# RET1 (stream S2-bodies, worker W12, EQ fuzz row 0x00cbc8f0) - a search function whose result the decomp dropped
# (docs/PATCHES.md "RET1").

@@ RET1 src/staging/blk_00ca0000_o2.cpp 0x00cbc8f0
# x86 0x00cbc8f0 (thiscall, `ret 4`): eax = [ecx+0x10] - 1; while eax >= 0, the byte [[ecx+0xc] + eax] is compared with
# the argument and the loop stops on equal; eax is decremented otherwise. It leaves through `pop esi; ret 4` with eax
# = the index found, or through the `js` exit with eax = -1: the function returns the last index of the byte (-1 when
# there is none) and writes nothing. The decomp loop computes that index into a local and returns void, so the loop
# has no effect and GCC deletes it (the native body is a bare `ret`); its caller (explosion_o2_nood_variant.cpp) already
# declares a result and indexes with it. Fix: return the index as `int` (the whole of eax). The definition's
# decoration changes (units_renames.tsv).
<<<
    void FUN_00cbc8f0(int arg);
===
    int FUN_00cbc8f0(int arg);
>>>
<<<
void FUN_00cbc8f0_cls::FUN_00cbc8f0(int aiValue)
===
int FUN_00cbc8f0_cls::FUN_00cbc8f0(int aiValue)
>>>
<<<
        } while (count >= 0);
    }
===
        } while (count >= 0);
    }
    return count;
>>>
